          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do VOC regulations differ between India, the EU, and the US for aerosol manufacturing?",
          "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "VOC (Volatile Organic Compound) regulations affecting aerosol propellant and solvent selection vary significantly. In the US, California's CARB (California Air Resources Board) sets the strictest limits, restricting LPG propellant usage in certain cosmetic aerosol categories. EU regulations under Directive 2004/42/EC set VOC limits for decorative and automotive aerosols, with HFC phase-down additionally affecting propellant selection. India currently does not have product-specific aerosol VOC regulations at the same level of detail, though CPCB governs ambient air quality standards and manufacturers targeting export markets must comply with destination-country VOC rules from the design stage." }
        },
